 AI model has the lowest latency?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite (Non-reasoning) has the lowest time to first token at 0.31s, followed by North Mini Code (0.40s) and Command A+ (0.40s)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which is the best open weights AI model?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GLM-5.3 (max) is the highest-ranked open weights model with an Intelligence Index score of 45. There are 62 open weights models out of 133 total evaluated."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the top open weights AI models?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The top open weights AI models by Intelligence Index are: 1. GLM-5.3 (max) (45), 2. Kimi K3 (max) (44), and 3. GLM-5.3-Flash (42)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which is the best reasoning model?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Fable 5.1 (Adaptive Reasoning, Max Effort, Default Fallback) leads among 115 reasoning models with an Intelligence Index score of 53. Reasoning models use extended thinking to work through complex problems before providing answers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are AI models compared on Artificial Analysis?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Models are compared across multiple dimensions including intelligence (quality), pricing, output speed (tokens per second), latency (time to first token), end-to-end response time, and context window size. Performance metrics are measured directly using standardized prompts across 644 models."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I compare a specific model against others?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Click on any model name or row in the charts to view its dedicated page with detailed metrics and direct comparisons against similar models. You can also use the model selector to customize which models appear in each chart."}}]}]